2026-05-07T06:07:55.264Z JOY-0169-6A comment.added "[x] New module crates/joy-cli/src/update_registry.rs with UpdateItem trait + RowMark enum (Ok / Stale / Info) + CheckRow / RefreshRow value types + all() returning Vec<Box<dyn UpdateItem>>.\n[x] Items implemented: VersionMarkerItem, GitignoreBlockItem, GitattributesBlockItem, MergeDriverItem, HooksPathItem, EmbeddedFilesItem (parameterised, three instances for HOOK_FILES / CONFIG_FILES / PROJECT_FILES), SecurityMdItem, ProjectYamlSchemaItem, AiToolItem (parameterised, four instances for claude / qwen / vibe / copilot).\n[x] commands/update.rs is now a thin orchestrator: iterate the registry by section, format rows joy-style, drive the binary self-update around it. run_check is comprehensive (every row), run_full_sync is terse (only changed rows + lazy section headers).\n[x] commands/auth.rs and commands/ai.rs lost their per-domain run_update_default / run_check_default / update_terse functions; the work moved into the registry items. They now expose only the helpers the items need (auth_state_pub, write_migrated_project, tool_display_name, tool_ids, is_tool_installed, is_tool_configured_pub, is_tool_stale_pub, refresh_tool_by_id, sync_gitignore_for_configured_tools).\n[x] commands/init.rs no longer routes through commands::auth; it calls security_md::render directly so a fresh init has SECURITY.md rendered without going through the registry.\n[x] AiToolItem reports 'installed, not configured' and 'not installed' as RowMark::Info so they no longer count toward the --check exit code.\n[x] 319 unit tests, 56 sanity bats green, clippy + fmt clean. Adding a new artefact now means: write one impl, append one entry in update_registry::all(); orchestrator and check pick it up automatically." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
